ysis (中毒性表皮坏死溶解症) [Data: Entities (15584, 15344, 15277); Relationships (9836, 9827)]. While剥脱性皮炎 is also associated with non-NSAID drugs like ethambutol [Data: Relationships (8306)], its repeated appearance in NSAID-related records underscores a pattern of dermatologic risk. These reactions are rare but potentially fatal, requiring immediate discontinuation of the offending agent and supportive care. Public health messaging and prescriber education are critical to early recognition and mitigation.\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to the documented life-threatening adverse reactions—including toxic epidermal necrolysis, exfoliative dermatitis, and myocardial infarction—associated with commonly prescribed NSAIDs in this community.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782127132, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1565, "prompt_tokens": 4178, "total_tokens": 5743, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"双氯芬酸钠缓释片 and 右布洛芬: NSAID Therapeutics and Associated Risks\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on two nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs)—双氯芬酸钠缓释片Ⅰ, 双氯芬酸钠缓释片IV, and 右布洛芬—and their therapeutic indications for musculoskeletal conditions such as shoulder periarthritis, sprains, low back pain, and tendinitis. These drugs are also associated with serious adverse reactions, including severe skin reactions like toxic epidermal necrolysis and exfoliative dermatitis, as well as cardiovascular risks such as myocardial infarction. Additionally, drug–drug interaction